Bean Scopes :
This topic answers When Spring creates a Bean, how many objects should it create?

Types of Bean Scopes:
1. Singleton Scope
--> This is the default scope in Spring:
@Component
public class Student {}
--> No scope specified.
--> Spring automatically uses:Singleton
--> Spring creates Only ONE Object and keeps reusing it.

Student s1 = context.getBean(Student.class);----
                                                |----> Same Object
Student s2 = context.getBean(Student.class);----

Advantages :
--> Less memory
--> Faster

2. Prototype Scope :

Student s1 = context.getBean(Student.class);----> Object1

Student s2 = context.getBean(Student.class);----> Object2

Difference Between Singleton and Prototype :
| Singleton     | Prototype                |
| ------------- | ------------------------ |
| One object    | New object every request |
| Default scope | Must be specified        |
| Less memory   | More memory              |

