Autowiring : It is the process by which Spring automatically injects dependencies into a bean.
Types of Autowiring :

1. Constructor Autowiring
@Component
public class Car 
{
    private Engine engine;
    public Car(Engine engine) 
    {
        this.engine = engine;
    }
}
--> Spring automatically injects Engine.

2. Setter Autowiring
@Component
public class Car 
{
    private Engine engine;
    @Autowired
    public void setEngine(Engine engine) 
    {
        this.engine = engine;
    }
}
--> Spring calls setEngine(engine) automatically.

3. Field Autowiring
@Component
public class Car 
{
    @Autowired
    private Engine engine;
}
--> Spring injects Engine directly into the field.

Java-based Configuration :

@Configuration : Marks a class as a Spring configuration class.
@Configuration
public class AppConfig {}
--> This class contains Spring configuration.

@ComponentScan : Tells Spring which package to scan for components.
@Configuration
@ComponentScan("com.teju")
public class AppConfig {}

@Bean : Used to create and register a bean manually.
@Configuration
public class AppConfig 
{
    @Bean
    public Engine engine() 
    {
        return new Engine();
    }
}

Step 1: Create a Normal Class
Start with:
public class AppConfig {}

Step 2: Tell Spring This Is a Configuration Class
@Configuration
public class AppConfig {}

Step 3: Tell Spring Where To Search //@ComponentScan("com.teju")
@Configuration
@ComponentScan("com.teju")
public class AppConfig {}

Step 4: Bean creation //@bean
@Bean
public Engine engine() 
{
    return new Engine();
}

Final Code :
@Configuration
@ComponentScan("com.teju")
public class AppConfig 
{
    @Bean
    public Engine engine() 
    {
        return new Engine();
    }
}
